{
  "contract": "m19-skills/3",
  "$comment": [
    "VERSIONED SKILLS, ADDITIVE TO m19-skills/2. /2 stays published and unchanged until no consumer reads it; this index is not yet read by any consumer (skill-registry spec, step 1).",
    "Selection by template is /2's rule: `common` is always selected and a template names the `specialisations` it wants; both now list skill NAMES, which key `skills`.",
    "Each skill has `versions`. A version pins its own `revision` (the analyser commit holding its bytes) and a `sha256` per file in `files`; exactly one file is the skill's SKILL.md and any other sits beside it.",
    "`compatibility`: `analyser` is the minimum analyser version; `authoring` is java | spring | any; `host` is mongoose | embedded | any; `mongoose` and `mongoosePlugins` are SEPARATE version ranges (space-separated comparators, all must hold, or `*`).",
    "For each selected skill a consumer takes the HIGHEST version that is not `yanked`, carries `evidence`, and whose compatibility contains the project's effective pins. No such version: the project gets none of that skill, never an incompatible one.",
    "A version without `evidence` is not selectable. `yanked: true` removes a version from selection without deleting it.",
    "1.0.0 of every skill is exactly its m19-skills/2 pin (same revision, same digests); its evidence is that pin. While /2 is served, CanonicalSkillsTest requires every /2 pin to appear here as a version with the same revision and digests."
  ],
  "common": [
    "load-audit-log",
    "guided-start",
    "point-at-the-fault"
  ],
  "specialisations": {
    "mongoose": {
      "why": "the processor is hosted by a Mongoose server",
      "skills": [
        "run-mongoose-server"
      ]
    },
    "embedded": {
      "why": "the processor runs in-process via DataFlowConnector",
      "skills": [
        "run-embedded"
      ]
    },
    "spring": {
      "why": "the graph is authored as Spring XML and compiled ahead of time",
      "skills": [
        "add-a-node"
      ]
    },
    "replay": {
      "why": "the project has a REAL replay entry point the bundle can name; without one, replay-a-run's TODO(bundle) cannot be substituted",
      "skills": [
        "replay-a-run"
      ]
    }
  },
